## Sizing

The panel fills the left sidebar's Git view on its own, as the [LeftSidebar](../left-sidebar/index.md#left-sidebar) says, never sharing it with the file tree, so there is no edge between them to drag. Its header, the branch with Pull and Push, sits at the view's top, the summary beneath it, the message box, Generate, and Commit along the view's bottom, and the commit notes fill the height between, however tall the window. It fills the sidebar's whole height, from beneath the ribbon to the window's bottom, whatever its contents: never only as tall as they need, and never leaving the rest of the view empty beneath it. With few notes or none, the space between the summary and the message box is simply empty, on the body's colour, and the message box, Generate, and Commit stay along the bottom.

